      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The feeling that you are fundamentally defined by this event is a heavy symptom of trauma, not necessarily the truth of your being. While the pain of the damage is real, the process of healing involves separating the action from your core identity. True repair involves owning the consequences, taking responsibility for the amends possible, and slowly allowing compassion for your own humanity to creep back in. Living with this means learning to carry the memory while building a path toward meaningful atonement.",
      "source": "target",
